# Files in here are only meant to be require()'d by a bootstrapped
# page (one that already loaded config/app.php) — several of them
# execute real logic immediately using functions/constants that only
# exist after that bootstrap has run. Hitting one directly does no
# harm to data, but it does throw an uncaught PHP error that can leak
# the server's file path. Simplest fix: never let a browser request
# reach these files at all.
<FilesMatch "\.php$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
Options -Indexes
